name 'ai-and-the-systems-that-power-it-lesson2-match-1'
title 'Component-Definition Match'
description 'Match the hardware component to its description or function'

question 'Motherboard'
answer 'Carries power and information between all the other parts. Does no thinking or storing of its own'

question 'CPU'
answer 'The main processor. Reads instructions and carries them out one at a time, in order, very fast'

question 'GPU'
answer 'A second processor built to do millions of small calculations all at once instead of one after another'

question 'RAM'
answer 'Holds whatever is open right now so the computer can reach it quickly. Empties the moment the power goes off'

question 'SSD'
answer 'Keeps files and programs in place even when the power is off, until something asks for them'

question 'Keyboard'
answer 'Sends letters, numbers, and commands into the computer when a person presses it'

question 'Monitor'
answer 'Displays the words and images the computer produced so a person can see them'

height '80'
allow_multiple_attempts true
